{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["If he comes in by himself, he goes out by himself — it states a general rule and then specifies. אם בגפו — he entered his master's house alone, meaning he does not yet have a wife who would enter with him. Or even if — his master gives him a wife — in any case he goes out by himself, for the wife his master gave him belongs to her master. And now I shall explain how: שאם בעל אשה הוא — he does not go out by himself, but rather his wife goes out with him. But — אם אדוניו יתן לו אשה וגו׳ — just as he came in by himself, so he goes out by himself. And it is speaking of a Canaanite maidservant whom his master handed over to him."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:19.097615858Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}